# CODEOWNERS — who reviews what.
#
# GitHub uses this file to auto-request reviews when a PR touches paths
# below. Combined with branch protection ("Require review from Code Owners"),
# it means:
#   - Anyone with write access can push a PR
#   - A PR touching site code / config / infra REQUIRES an owner review
#   - A PR touching ONLY recipe markdown auto-approves (with the right rule)
#
# Replace @your-github-handle with your actual GitHub username.

# Default: everything requires owner review
*                                    @your-github-handle

# Recipe content — no code, safe to let content editors self-merge
# (still governed by branch protection; see COLLABORATION.md)
/src/content/recipes/                @your-github-handle @amy-github-handle

# Infrastructure / config / secrets — owner only
/.github/                            @your-github-handle
/astro.config.mjs                    @your-github-handle
/package.json                        @your-github-handle
/package-lock.json                   @your-github-handle
/src/lib/config.ts                   @your-github-handle
